An agent moves on a {{ n }}x{{ n }} grid. Its state is its cell (x = row, y = column; (0,0) is the top-left corner, x grows downward, y grows rightward) plus one flag per goal.

- The agent starts at (0,0) with every goal flag false.
- Goals must be visited in order: {% for g in goals %}goal {{ g.k }} at ({{ g.row }},{{ g.col }}){% if not loop.last %}, then {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Flag g1 becomes true when the agent enters goal 1's cell, and flag gk (k > 1) becomes true when it enters goal k's cell while g(k-1) is already true. Entering a goal's cell early, before its turn, violates the ordering requirements.
- Each step the agent picks an action (up, right, down or left). It moves in the chosen direction with probability {{ prob_forward }}, and slips 90 degrees to the left or right of it with probability {{ prob_slip_left }} and {{ prob_slip_right }}. For example, choosing down means down {{ prob_forward }}, right {{ prob_slip_left }}, left {{ prob_slip_right }}.
- Moving off the grid leaves the agent where it is. Static obstacles{% if static %} at {{ static | join(', ') }}{% endif %} can never be entered: a move into one also leaves the agent where it is.
{% if cycle %}
- A moving obstacle patrols the cells {{ cycle | join(' -> ') }} and then repeats, advancing one position per agent step. It starts at {{ cycle[0] }}. Its cells can be entered, but sharing a cell with the obstacle at the same time counts as a collision. The policy cannot observe where the obstacle currently is.
{% endif %}
- The agent keeps moving after it reaches the last goal.
